  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "ICML and REALM propose frameworks to address challenges in long-term memory management for LLM agents, enabling continuous improvement through interactive and reconsolidation mechanisms. Video understanding agents improve their evidence acquisition by harnessing evolution and utilizing EgoGears. Agent skills matter through inferred proprietary skills and hierarchical skill graphs, while harness evolution improves performance with budget-aware frameworks.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "ICML and REALM propose frameworks to address challenges in long-term memory management for LLM agents, enabling continuous improvement through interactive and reconsolidation mechanisms.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Video understanding agents improve their evidence acquisition through harness evolution and utilize EgoGears to diagnose transfer of local video understanding across encounters.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A 13-28 point gender gap and 18-25 point drop in video-LLMs' performance are observed despite no improvement in video quality.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
